  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscRC 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A research team is reviewing patient samples from past studies to explore
    new ideas for cancer treatments. You help track consent and ensure the team follows
    ethical and privacy standards.\n\n<b>Research coordinators are responsible for
    making sure any patient samples\u2014like blood or tissue\u2014are handled properly
    and used only for approved purposes.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Even in the early discovery, research coordinators are responsible
    for making sure that all patient samples are collected, stored, and used in an
    ethical and secure way by confirming that every sample was donated with informed
    consent, removing personal details to protect patient privacy, and ensuring samples
    are used only for approved studies. Their careful oversight helps keep research
    safe, responsible, and focused on advancing treatments that truly benefit patients
    and families.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
